  helpLongHow_admin_members_tiers: '① Pick store, date, and filters first, then open a row in the list or a detail form.\n② Fill required fields with correct types (dates, numbers, selects), and re-check amounts and approvers before Save, Submit, or Approve.\n③ If data looks stale, refresh; if it persists, check concurrency and month-end rules with ops or accounting to avoid double booking.\n④ Export and print only with appropriate rights; follow your org’s data-handling and retention policy.',
  helpLongWhat_admin_sales_management:
    'Roll up and compare POS store sales across time, channel, payment method, menu, delivery apps, and store dimensions. Use the left rail to pick a submenu (performance analytics, store comparison rollups, POS operations including the business-day start time, forecasts/reports), then pick a topic inside it. Under “POS operations”, head office can set the org-wide Bangkok-time default for when a new POS business day begins; store managers and franchisees can save per-store overrides for stores tied to their login (including allowed extra stores). Overrides drive that store’s POS “today”, settlement windows, and daily buckets. Use the dine-in / takeout / delivery toggles at the top to match how your org defines “sales in scope.” On the admin web path the default landing may open on store comparison; when opened from POS, offline mode may read cached aggregates. Figures can differ from accounting definitions depending on close time, voids, discounts, and sync delay—document the date range, store, and order-type scope you used for any external report.',
  helpLongHow_admin_sales_management:
    '[Scope] ① Set the date range and period grain (year/month/week/day/hour/day-of-week, etc.), then run the query action so charts and tables populate.\n② Store: head-office roles can select multiple stores or enable compare mode; a single store may reflect your login scope.\n③ Order type: toggle dine-in, takeout, and delivery to align totals.\n[Left menu] ④ Performance analytics: best for drilling why totals moved (period, channel, payment, menu, delivery).\n⑤ Store comparison: pivot-style views across stores, time, and categories.\n⑥ POS operations: save the org default or pick a store and save an override (Bangkok). Remove override to fall back to the org default. POS terminals pick changes up on the next settings fetch; daily aggregates and settlement ranges follow the effective boundary per store.\n⑦ Forecasts & reports: MoM, forecasts, and overview-style topics for meetings.\n[Validation] ⑧ Large day-over-day swings: check promos, channel mix, discounts, or missing close; cross-check POS settlement for the same store/date.\n⑨ If an offline banner appears, re-query after connectivity returns.\n⑩ Open this long help from the tab bar “This screen / Help” or the URL help mode.',
