  helpLongWhat_admin_payroll: 'This screen is for “Payroll (screen has its own help tab when applicable)”. The exact store scope, tabs, and fields depend on your role, org, and process (head office vs franchise, accounting close, etc.). External systems (POS, bank, cloud) may have replication delay or concurrency rules; refresh before you rely on balances. Use PII, payroll, and tax data with least privilege, and be careful with exports and screenshots outside approved channels.',
  helpLongHow_admin_payroll: '① Pick store, date, and filters first, then open a row in the list or a detail form.\n② Fill required fields with correct types (dates, numbers, selects), and re-check amounts and approvers before Save, Submit, or Approve.\n③ If data looks stale, refresh; if it persists, check concurrency and month-end rules with ops or accounting to avoid double booking.\n④ Export and print only with appropriate rights; follow your org’s data-handling and retention policy.',
  helpLongWhat_admin_receivable_payable: 'This screen is for “A/R, A/P, and aging by counterparty”. The exact store scope, tabs, and fields depend on your role, org, and process (head office vs franchise, accounting close, etc.). External systems (POS, bank, cloud) may have replication delay or concurrency rules; refresh before you rely on balances. Use PII, payroll, and tax data with least privilege, and be careful with exports and screenshots outside approved channels.',
  helpLongHow_admin_receivable_payable: '① Pick store, date, and filters first, then open a row in the list or a detail form.\n② Fill required fields with correct types (dates, numbers, selects), and re-check amounts and approvers before Save, Submit, or Approve.\n③ If data looks stale, refresh; if it persists, check concurrency and month-end rules with ops or accounting to avoid double booking.\n④ Export and print only with appropriate rights; follow your org’s data-handling and retention policy.',
  helpLongWhat_admin_expense_management: 'This screen is for “Expenses, receipts, and approvals”. When the same cash movement also exists as a bank withdrawal, pick one accounting path so journals do not double-post. Store scope, tabs, and fields depend on your role, org, and process (head office vs franchise, accounting close, etc.). External systems (POS, bank, cloud) may have replication delay or concurrency rules; refresh before you rely on balances. Use PII, payroll, and tax data with least privilege, and be careful with exports and screenshots outside approved channels.',
  helpLongHow_admin_expense_management: '① Pick store, date, and filters first, then open a row in the list or a detail form.\n② Fill required fields with correct types (dates, numbers, selects), and re-check amounts and approvers before Save, Submit, or Approve.\n③ If data looks stale, refresh; if it persists, check concurrency and month-end rules with ops or accounting to avoid double booking.\n④ Export and print only with appropriate rights; follow your org’s data-handling and retention policy.\n⑤ (Bank link) Only unlinked withdrawals are offered. If that bank row was already saved as Expense or Purchase payment, the bank side may have posted expense/cash or payable/cash; linking the same row again from Expense Management can double-hit cash (and expense or payables). Align the withdrawal category with your SOP or ask accounting; see Bank Transactions help step ⑤ and the banner on that page.',
  helpLongWhat_admin_petty_cash: 'This screen is for “Petty cash book and vouchers”. The exact store scope, tabs, and fields depend on your role, org, and process (head office vs franchise, accounting close, etc.). External systems (POS, bank, cloud) may have replication delay or concurrency rules; refresh before you rely on balances. Use PII, payroll, and tax data with least privilege, and be careful with exports and screenshots outside approved channels.',
  helpLongHow_admin_petty_cash: '① Pick store, date, and filters first, then open a row in the list or a detail form.\n② Fill required fields with correct types (dates, numbers, selects), and re-check amounts and approvers before Save, Submit, or Approve.\n③ If data looks stale, refresh; if it persists, check concurrency and month-end rules with ops or accounting to avoid double booking.\n④ Export and print only with appropriate rights; follow your org’s data-handling and retention policy.',
  helpLongWhat_admin_bank_transactions: 'This screen is for “Bank CSV import, period query, invoice flags, memo rules, and fixed expenses”. Deposits tie to revenue/collections; withdrawals tie to expenses, vendor payments, transfers, etc., and can update receivables/payables. If you will later link the same withdrawal from Expense Management, the category you choose here controls whether a bank auto-journal runs—wrong combo risks double posting; read step ⑤ below. Scope, roles, and bank feed delay vary; refresh before you rely on balances. Use PII and tax data with least privilege; be careful with exports outside approved channels.',
  helpLongHow_admin_bank_transactions: '① Pick store, date, and filters first, then open a row in the list or a detail form.\n② POS auto-journal (card/delivery→1130): deposit category must be Sales collection (receivable_receive) with store and sales date—not revenue_* (double revenue). Card/delivery fees: post on POS settlement or use Channel settlement on the deposit row (NET+FEE clears 1130).\n③ Fill required fields with correct types (dates, numbers, selects), and re-check amounts and approvers before Save, Submit, or Approve.\n④ If data looks stale, refresh; if it persists, check concurrency and month-end rules with ops or accounting to avoid double booking.\n⑤ Export and print only with appropriate rights; follow your org’s data-handling and retention policy.\n⑥ (Overlap with Expense Management — withdraw category) Transfer, loan, advance, correction, and unclassified do not auto-post a P&L journal on save, so they pair well with “link this bank line” payment from Expense Management (payable settlement posts when you pay). Expense (and Fixed, saved as expense) already posts expense/cash—do not also link that same line as an expense-accrual bank payment (choose one workflow). Purchase payment already posts payable/cash—do not also run the same vendor payment twice from Expense Management; use one path.\n⑦ If the withdrawal exists first and there is no accrual yet, office users can use “Register expense from bank transaction” to create and link in one go.',
  helpLongWhat_admin_depreciation: 'This screen is for “Depreciation, assets, and disposals”. The exact store scope, tabs, and fields depend on your role, org, and process (head office vs franchise, accounting close, etc.). External systems (POS, bank, cloud) may have replication delay or concurrency rules; refresh before you rely on balances. Use PII, payroll, and tax data with least privilege, and be careful with exports and screenshots outside approved channels.',
